dded cheese, sour cream, diced avocado, cilantro) \n\nInstructions:\n\n1. Preheat oven to 350°F. Place chicken breasts on a lined baking sheet and bake for approximately 30 minutes or until cooked through. \n2. Once chicken is done, use two forks to shred the meat and set aside. \n3. In a large pot, heat olive oil over medium heat. Add diced onions and bell peppers and sauté for 5-7 minutes until softened. \n4. Add minced garlic, chili powder, cumin, paprika, oregano, coriander, and salt. Stir to combine and sauté for an additional 1-2 minutes. \n5. Add black beans, diced tomatoes, tomato sauce, frozen corn, chicken broth, and enchilada sauce to the pot. Stir to combine.\n6. Bring the soup to a boil, then reduce heat to low and let simmer for 20-30 minutes.\n7. Serve hot with optional toppings such as shredded cheese, sour cream, diced avocado, and cilantro. \n\nOptional variations: \n- Add some diced jalapeños for extra heat \n- Use different beans such as pinto or kidney beans \n- Substitute chicken breasts for pre-cooked shredded chicken from a rotisserie chicken. \n- Use vegetable broth instead of chicken broth for a vegetarian option.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nCan you tell me more about the different kinds of toppings I can add? Also, could you suggest a side dish that would go well with this soup?<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\nSure, here are some toppings that would go well with Chicken Enchilada Soup:\n\n-Shredded cheese (e.g. Cheddar, Monterey Jack, pepper jack)\n-Sour cream or Greek yogurt \n-Diced avocado \n-Fresh cilantro \n-Sliced jalapeños or green onions \n-Tortilla chips or strips \n\nAs for a side dish, some options that would complement the flavors of the soup include:\n\n-Cornbread \n-Side salad with a tangy vinaigrette \n-Grilled or sautéed vegetables such as zucchini, bell peppers, or onions \n-Black bean and corn salad \n\nI hope this helps!<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nCan you tell me more about how to make the cornbread and what ingredients I shoul","tokens":["<|im_start|>","system","\n","You"," are"," a"," helpful"," assistant",".","<|im_end|>","\n","<|im_start|>","user","\n","Provide"," a"," list"," of"," necessary"," ingredients"," for"," the"," chicken"," ench","il","ada"," soup"," and"," the"," measurements"," required"," for"," each","."," Include"," a"," step","-by","-step"," process"," for"," preparing"," the"," soup",","," including"," how"," to"," cook"," and"," shred"," the"," chicken"," and"," when"," to"," add"," each"," ingredient"," to"," the"," pot","."," Also",","," specify"," any"," particular"," cooking"," techniques",","," such"," as"," sa","ut","é","ing"," or"," simmer","ing",","," and"," how"," long"," to"," cook"," the"," soup"," for","."," Finally",","," include"," any"," optional"," toppings"," or"," variations"," for"," the"," soup",".","<|im_end|>","\n","<|im_start|>","assistant","\n","Chicken"," En","ch","il","ada"," Soup"," Ingredients",":\n\n","-","1"," lb"," bone","less",","," skin","less"," chicken"," breasts","\n","-","1"," tbsp"," olive"," oil","\n","-","1"," medium"," onion",","," diced"," \n","-","2"," bell"," peppers",","," diced"," \n","-","3"," garlic"," cloves",","," minced"," \n","-","2"," tsp"," chili"," powder"," \n","-","1"," tsp"," ground"," c","umin","\n","-","1","/","4"," tsp"," pap","rika"," \n","-","1","/","4"," tsp"," o","reg","ano"," \n","-","1","/","4"," tsp"," cor","i","ander"," \n","-","1","/","4"," tsp"," salt"," \n","-","1"," can"," black"," beans",","," drained"," and"," rins","ed"," \n","-","1"," can"," diced"," tomatoes"," with"," green"," ch","ilies"," \n","-","1"," can"," tomato"," sauce"," \n","-","1"," cup"," frozen"," corn"," \n","-","4"," cups"," chicken"," broth"," \n","-","1","/","2"," cup"," ench","il","ada"," sauce"," \n","-","Optional"," toppings"," (","e",".g","."," Sh","redd","ed"," cheese",","," sour"," cream",","," diced"," avocado",","," cil","antro",")"," \n\n","Instructions",":\n\n","1","."," Pre","heat"," oven"," to"," "