and has implemented various programs and resources to support their students in dealing with stress and anxiety. These include:\n\n1. Counseling and Psychological Services (CAPS): CAPS provides students with access to confidential counseling, therapy, and psychiatric services. They offer individual and group therapy sessions, as well as workshops and support groups.\n\n2. Student Health Service: The Student Health Service offers medical care and support for physical and mental health needs. They have a team of healthcare professionals, including doctors, nurses, and mental health clinicians.\n\n3. Penn Wellness: Penn Wellness is a university-wide initiative that promotes health and well-being for students, faculty, and staff. They offer various programs and resources, including mindfulness meditation sessions, stress management workshops, and relaxation yoga classes.\n\n4. Student Assistance Program: The Student Assistance Program is a free, confidential counseling service that provides students with support and guidance for personal and academic issues. The program offers assessment, counseling, and referral services for a wide range of issues, including stress, anxiety, and depression.\n\n5. Peer Counseling: Peer Counseling is a non-profit, student-run organization that provides confidential support to students. Trained peer counselors provide a safe and supportive space for students to talk about their concerns and provide referrals to other resources.\n\nOverall, the University of Pennsylvania is committed to providing a comprehensive range of mental health resources and support to help students manage their stress and anxiety. Students can access these resources through various channels, including the university website, email, and phone.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nCan you give me specific examples of workshops and support groups offered by Counseling and Psychological Services (CAPS)?<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\nSure, here are some examples of workshop